{"ts": "2026-10-13T21:42:37+0900", "unit_id": "wittgenstein-1953-investigations/ch04-private", "state": "p3_queued", "reason": "deterministic checks fail after P2", "loop": 1, "issues": [{"severity": "major", "check": "C", "where": "L3 §§285–312, Concepts, Canonical instances", "problem": "From §285 on, page references drift one page too high. Several point to pdf 140, which does not exist (the unit ends at pdf 139). For example §288 is on pdf 134, §293 on 135–136, §304 on 137–138, §305–307 on 138, and §309–312 on 139.", "evidence": "pdf 134 = §285–288; pdf 135 = §289–293 start; pdf 136 = §293 end–298; pdf 137 = §299–304 start; pdf 138 = §304 end–308 start; pdf 139 = §308 end–312"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "C", "where": "L3 §§281–284", "problem": "References are off by one: §281–282 begin on pdf 132, and §283–284 are on pdf 133.", "evidence": "pdf 132 (103e) contains §281 and the start of §282; pdf 133 (104e) contains the end of §282, §283 and §284"}, {"severity": "critical", "check": "A", "where": "L3 §312 final note and Reading notes", "problem": "The digest says §312 continues beyond the supplied pages. The source does not say this; the last supplied page ends at 'infer important properties of the objects from them'.", "evidence": "pdf 139 (last lines of §312)"}, {"severity": "critical", "check": "A", "where": "L3 §266", "problem": "The claim that 'Looking at a clock in one's imagination' has no fixed use is not in the source. The source gives only the bare parenthesis.", "evidence": "pdf 129, §266: '(Looking at a clock in one's imagination.)'"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "A", "where": "L3 §259", "problem": "The source asks a question ('Are the rules ... impressions of rules?'), but the digest turns it into a flat assertion.", "evidence": "pdf 128, §259"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "A", "where": "L3 §243, §249, §297, §293 intuition note", "problem": "Small distortions of the source. In §243 the 'since he hears resolutions' clause belongs to the prediction remark. In §249 the source asks whether we are over-hasty. In §297 the source asks a question rather than calling the insistence 'absurd'. In the §293 note, 'appears the same way in every public use' is not what the text says; the text says it cancels 'whatever it is'.", "evidence": "pdf 124 (§243), pdf 125 (§249), pdf 136 (§297), pdf 135–136 (§293)"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "D", "where": "L3 §312", "problem": "The sentence 'I can exhibit the visual impression to myself as little or as well as the sensation of pain' is omitted.", "evidence": "pdf 139, §312"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "E", "where": "Toy example", "problem": "The sentence 'Fraction of assignments the record singles out: 1/64 only if we pretend...' is muddled and gives a misleading fraction. The count 4×4×4=64 is correct.", "evidence": "Arithmetic check: 4³ = 64; the record is identical for all assignments"}, {"severity": "minor", "check": "G", "where": "L1", "problem": "L1 has 124 words, over the 120-word limit.", "evidence": "Automatic format check"}, {"severity": "major", "check": "G", "problem": "contains 'I cannot'"}]}
